.TH usm 1 "3 August 2026" "Version 2.4.1" "USM NPM INSTALLER"
.SH NAME
.B usm-npm-install
\- The USM NPM installer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B usm-install-npm
PACKAGE
[VERSION]
[APP-NAME]
.SH DESCRIPTION
This is a utility for installing and updating software distributed via npm.
This creates an application directory within USM, installs the package into
it, and creates symlinks for all binaries that the package provides.
.IP
.B
usm-install-npm typescript latest
.PP
Internally, this command does three things:
.IP
1. Executes "usm add typescript npm" to create a prefix.
.IP
2. Executes "npm install typescript@latest" within that preifx.
.IP
3. Creates a bin/ directory within that prefix and adds symlinks to every file
in the node_modules/.bin/ directory.
.PP
After usm-install-npm finishes, dot-source your .usm-env file to put all the package's commands on your $PATH:
.IP
.B
$ tsc --version
.br
Version 5.2.2
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
PACKAGE
The name of the npm package. Required.
.TP
VERSION
The version of the npm package. Optional, if not provided it is assumed to be
.B latest
.TP
APP-NAME
The name of the USM directory to install the package into. Optional, if not
provided the app name is derived from PACKAGE by replacing dots and slashes
with underscores.
.IP
This option is intended for two situations. If the package name conflicts with
some other USM application, you need to provide a different app name.
.IP
You can also use this to install multiple npm packages into the same directory.
Each USM application gets a separate node_modules/ directory, which is normally
what you want to avoid dependency conflicts. However, if multiple packages
share a large dependency, you can save space by installing them into the same
USM app. Binaries from
.I 
all 
packages are still symlinked into the bin/ directory.
.SH EXAMPLES
Install the latest version of typescript into $USM_PATH/typescript/npm.
.IP
.B
usm-install-npm typescript
.P
Once installed, you can run the command with the same package name
(and app name, if you gave it the first time) to upgrade the existing
package to a new version.
.P
Install a specific version of typescript into $USM_PATH/tsc/npm.
.IP
.B
usm-install-npm typescript 3.9.4 tsc
.SH LIMITATIONS
Packages managed by usm-install-npm do not work with USM's version handling.
Each application managed by usm-install-npm has a single
.B
npm
version, no matter the version of the underlying npm package. While you can
install the same package into different USM apps, only one of them will appear
on your $PATH. All other versions must be invoked using
.B
usm exec
or their full paths.
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
USM_PATH
Controls where this script finds the software managed by USM.
